<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baz Bahadur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1555">1555</a>–<a href="/years/1561">1561</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baz Bahadur was the last sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa">Malwa</a>, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandu">Mandu</a> in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. More devoted to music than to war, he is remembered for his romance with the singer Rupmati, celebrated in later poetry and painting. In 1561 the Mughal general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adham-khan">Adham Khan</a> defeated him and took Mandu, and Rupmati took her own life. Baz Bahadur later entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akbar">Akbar</a>'s service.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baz-bahadur.jpg" alt="Baz Bahadur" width="320" height="477" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:B%C3%A1z_Bah%C3%A1dur_and_R%C3%BApmat%C3%AD_on_horses_with_attendants.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
